13
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
The Hunt is a 2020 American satirical action horror film directed by
Craig Zobel and written by Nick Cuse and Damon Lindelof.

14
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
The film stars Betty Gilpin, Hilary Swank, Ike Barinholtz, and Emma Roberts.

15
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Jason Blum was a producer under his Blumhouse
Productions banner, along with Lindelof.

16
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Zobel and Lindelof have said that the film is intended as a satire on the
profound political divide between the American left and right.

17
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
It is about a group of elites who kidnap working-class people to hunt them.

18
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The film was first announced in March 2018, and the cast signed on a year later.

19
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Filming took place in New Orleans.

20
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
The film was originally scheduled for release on September 27, 2019.

21
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
However, as a result of the El Paso and Dayton mass shootings in early
August 2019, Universal Pictures decided to delay it.

22
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
The Hunt was released in theaters in the United States on March 13, 2020, by
Universal Pictures and received mixed reviews from critics.

23
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:46,000
The onset of the COVID-19 pandemic resulted in the closure of most theaters within a week of the film's
release, which resulted in the film underperforming at the box office, grossing only $12.4 million.

24
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Universal made The Hunt available digitally on March 20.

25
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
The film explores themes of dark comedy, gore, satire, murder, death game.

26
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
The tone is dark and intense.
